.TH "Hyprshot" "1" "15. March 2026" "Gustash" "documentation"
.SH "NAME "
Hyprshot
.SH "Synopsis "
\fBhyprshot\fP [options ..] [\-m [mode] .. ] \-\- [command]
.SH "DESCRIPTION "
\fPhyprshot\fP is a screenshot application for the Hyprland desktop environment and window manager. It acts as a simplification of versions with grim and slurp, to make it easier to use.
.SS "Options "
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fP
show help message
.TP
\fB\-m, \-\-mode\fP
chooses mode. Must be one of: output, window, region, active, OUTPUT_NAME
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output\-folder\fP
directory in which to save the screenshot (temporary)
.TP
\fB\-f, \-\-filename\fP
the file name of the resulting screenshot
.TP
\fB\-z, \-\-freeze\fP
freeze the screen when taking the screenshot
.TP
\fB\-d, \-\-debug\fP
print debug info
.TP
\fB\-s, \-\-silent\fP
don't send a notification when screenshot is saved
.TP
\fB\-r, \-\-raw\fP
output raw image data to stdout
.TP
\fB\-t, \-\-notif\-timeout\fP
notification timeout in milliseconds (default 5000)
.TP
\fB\-\-clipboard\-only\fB
copy screenshot to clipboard and don't save image in disk
.TP
\fB\-\- [command]\fP
open screenshot with a command of your choosing. e.g. hyprshot \-m window \-\- mirage
